{"chapter": 4, "sha256": "0dac28a0202c26fbc9df9d98a68d752c3eceaf43d10652907827dd24b25c9e42", "voice": {"voice_id": "ppLqTilh7rH7fbUVlXsf", "name": "David - Documentary", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.5, "similarity_boost": 0.8, "style": 0.0, "use_speaker_boost": true}}, "source": "docs/script.md", "files": {"narration": {"file": "ch4.mp3", "text": "Egypt's own records count back further than its kings.\n\nA papyrus in Turin, copied about 1250 BCE, lists the kings back to the first, Menes, and before him gods, spirits and the Followers of Horus, who reigned, on its likeliest reading, for more than thirteen thousand years. The Egyptians called that beginning sep tepi, the First Time. Hancock and Bauval read it as memory, not myth.\n\nA stela beside the Great Pyramid has Khufu finding a temple \"beside the house of the Sphinx\", so the Sphinx, they argue, was already there before Khafre.\n\nNone of these texts gives a date. So they looked for one in the sky.", "seconds": 49.21, "alignment": {"characters": ["E", "g", "y", "p", "t", "'", "s", " ", "o", "w", "n", " ", "r", "e", "c", "o", "r", "d", "s", " ", "c", "o", "u", "n", "t", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", " ", "f", "u", "r", "t", "h", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "k", "i", "n", "g", "s", ".", "\n", "\n", "A", " ", "p", "a", "p", "y", "r", "u", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "T", "u", "r", "i", "n", ",", " ", "c", "o", "p", "i", "e", "d", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "1", "2", "5", "0", " ", "B", "C", "E", ",", " ", "l", "i", "s", "t", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "k", "i", "n", "g", "s", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "i", "r", "s", "t", ",", " ", "M", "e", "n", "e", "s", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "b", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", " ", "h", "i", "m", " ", "g", "o", "d", "s", ",", " ", "s", "p", "i", "r", "i", "t", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "F", "o", "l", "l", "o", "w", "e", "r", "s", " ", "o", "f", 